request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" could mean several different format changes, and existing format tests pin down the current output. I need a concrete target before I can write a testable contract and decide which existing tests may change.)
governor asks: What should "easier to read" mean for the todo list output? Some options (pick any, or describe your own):
1. Checkbox markers per line, e.g. "[x] 3. Buy milk (due 2024-05-01)" vs "[ ] 4. Call mom".
2. Aligned columns: right-padded IDs so titles line up, and due dates in their own column.
3. Group or sort: open todos first, then done; or sort by due date.
4. A header and/or summary line, e.g. "3 open, 2 done".
5. A friendly message when the list is empty, e.g. "No todos."
6. Colour (ANSI) for done/overdue items. This would need a way to turn it off, e.g. when output isn't a terminal.
Also, should the confirmation text for add/complete change too (e.g. "Added #4: Call mom"), or only the list output?

